From 8868f2c150fc0b078116c56ac964c64e7b1bc408 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:19:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] Runner: a player's tag instead of their label

Gibax: if no tag, keep the 1P/2P label; else the player's tag. A racer a
player drives with a tag (SRNP_TAGS) now shows the tag in place of its
label, centred on it, a third of the way down, at twice its texel size;
no tag, or a CPU: the label as before (nP, COM). The routine is 79 words.

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats, tags on 5 seats): 29 checksums equal, 0
divergences in JIT64; the untagged seats keep 7P.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp | 36 +++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 src/runtime/srnp_labels.hpp |  7 ++++---
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp b/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp
index 14c17b8..1c3aea5 100644
--- a/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp
@@ -64,25 +64,27 @@ constexpr std::array<Patch, 4> kPatches = {{
      {0x89FE00BD, 0x55EF3E30, 0x53EF2676, 0x3DEF8000, 0x39EF2E00, 0x60000000}, 6},
     {0x8042F830, {0x4BBD8F9D}, {0x4BBD5511}, 1},  // bl 0x800087CC -> bl the routine (1P)
 }};
-// The routine saves r3-r9 and f1 (the quad's arguments), then:
-// 1. the label: our texture holds 5P-8P only; for any other label ((r15 & 0xC0) != 0x40, the table
-//    being 0x100-aligned), the game's quad with the game's atlas (bl 0x800087CC); for ours, it binds
-//    kEntry to texmap 0 (bl 0x8007D1EC), draws the quad, binds the game's current texture again
-//    (lwz r4,-0x7708(r13); li r3,0; bl 0x80053C54);
-// 2. the player's tag (not for a CPU: r15 & 0x80): if tag k ((r15 >> 4) & 7) has a width in
-//    kTagTable, a second quad over the label, centred, from the tags' texture (kTagEntry) with the
-//    table's UVs, in white; then the game's texture again.
+// The routine saves r3-r9 and f1 (the quad's arguments), then (Gibax: "if no tag we keep the 1P/2P,
+// else we put the player's tag"):
+// - a racer a player drives (not a CPU: r15 & 0x80) with a tag (tag k = (r15 >> 4) & 7 has a width
+//   in kTagTable): the tag instead of the label, from the tags' texture (kTagEntry) with the table's
+//   UVs, centred on the label, a third of the way down, twice its texel size, in white;
+// - otherwise the label: our texture holds 5P-8P only; for any other label ((r15 & 0xC0) != 0x40,
+//   the table being 0x100-aligned), the game's quad with the game's atlas (bl 0x800087CC); for ours,
+//   it binds kEntry to texmap 0 (bl 0x8007D1EC) and draws the quad;
+// then binds the game's current texture again (lwz r4,-0x7708(r13); li r3,0; bl 0x80053C54).
