 // The players' tags (SRNP_TAGS=TAG0,TAG1,... : seat k = racer k): a texture of ours too,
 // 128x128 C4, one 16-texel row per seat, zero in the file), written by the runner with our own pixel
diff --git a/src/runtime/srnp_labels.hpp b/src/runtime/srnp_labels.hpp
index d59eb54..f83ae96 100644
--- a/src/runtime/srnp_labels.hpp
+++ b/src/runtime/srnp_labels.hpp
@@ -17,9 +17,10 @@
 //   section: code in low memory hangs the game); for 5P..8P, it binds our texture
 //   (the game's own loader, 0x8007D1EC, given a texture entry of ours) around the game's quad
 //   function (0x800087CC), then binds the game's texture again (0x80053C54).
-// - the players' tags (SRNP_TAGS=TAG0,TAG1,... : seat k = racer k, up to 8 characters): a second quad
-//   over the label of a racer a player drives, from a second texture of ours in the block (128x128 C4,
-//   zero in the file) that the runner writes with its own pixel font; none for a CPU.
+// - the players' tags (SRNP_TAGS=TAG0,TAG1,... : seat k = racer k, up to 8 characters): a racer a
+//   player drives with a tag shows the tag instead of its label (no tag, or a CPU: the label), from a
+//   second texture of ours in the block (128x128 C4, zero in the file) that the runner writes with its
+//   own pixel font.
 // The table and the entry live in low memory the game leaves at zero (0x80002E00-0x80002F40); the
 // tags' entry and UV table after the routine (0x80004F00-0x80005000).
 // Without the block (no mod, another language), the game's code is put back. SRNP_ETIQUETTES=0
